codex
Phase 2 report is written to [pretty-link-phase2.codex.json](/Volumes/External_Disk/timo/WORDPRESS-PLUGIN-RESEARCH/reports/phase2/pretty-link-phase2.codex.json).

Result: no Patchstack-eligible `TP` or `REVIEW` survived source validation. I recorded 7 rejected candidates in `negative_findings` and 1 `out_of_scope` hardening issue for disabled TLS verification on outbound service calls. The main refuted themes were Semgrep over-taint on fixed plugin option keys, the token-gated bookmarklet route, the public invoice view requiring possession of a Stripe session ID, and public-looking routes that still remain admin-gated by nonce/session checks.

Validation: `jq` parsed the JSON successfully.
